      "message": "Yeah, if the new behavior is needed for third-party streams, they\u0027d have to override this.\n\nIn practice I can\u0027t find any custom streams that hold all the data in a continuous memory block.  If that behavior is needed, we have `SkMemoryStream`, which is flexible enough to support most use cases (owned/non-owned data, pre/post allocated, etc) -- so I\u0027d argue clients should just use that instead of attempting to reinvent.",
